tƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;V6pqG-XxehBEIo07BWI0Epd9cs3Ujr-4R9zoKA-JhUwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka0ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;KJ17SPCW-xBqjT_u8VQkHjjYfex3YwpOe0wVICN-31Aƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka0ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;YK1xBrow7udN0niP6rQU-2MhSg__Flc9kfwum2RwR0Qƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkhstandardƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;DcZKPJIaXKs08PnoFjDiwE6xIi9XocCg3lwuxvtcv9gƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkhstandardƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;wFNLRV00uYSDlwu6MFfNhjySiPifgaEgXUC3iJS1-o0ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx$a5df8ada-f631-48b4-ada6-3977313058e5ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;V3gXUqHv4r66JOKwMt8SCFhAPol2C4WnnUNi4ZpVr90ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkyAfter seven years during which the original GitHub repository sat frozen at its last commit, NextBSD has returned to active developmentâ€”under new management, with a new repository separate from the original, and the same founding purpose: porting Apple's open-source Darwin code into the FreeBSD ecosystem. [The Register's FOSS desk reported the revival on July 18, 2026.](https://www.theregister.com/os-platforms/2026/07/18/nextbsd-returns-to-dollop-apple-source-on-freebsd/5273788)

NextBSD was started in 2015 by Jordan Hubbard, a co-founder of FreeBSD. The plan from the beginning was to port components of Apple's Darwin OS to FreeBSD. Darwin is the Unix foundation on which macOS and Apple's other operating systems are built; it is open source, with its code available directly from GitHub. Bridging that codebase into FreeBSD required sustained porting effortâ€”work that exists only as long as someone is actively doing it.

## NextBSD Returns: Apple Darwin Source Porting Under New FreeBSD Stewardship

The developer who revived the project is Joe Maloney, known on GitHub as pkgdemon. Maloney is already recognized in BSD circles: he built the Gershwin desktop environment for GhostBSD, which The Register previously covered. Shortly after that coverage, Maloney approached the NextBSD maintainers and asked if he could take over the project. He had a relatively minor role in the originalâ€”his commits are visible in the project's historyâ€”and the maintainers agreed.

The new GitHub repository is distinct from the archived original, which remains accessible with its history intact. The revived project also includes a project history page crediting the contributors behind the original effort, including the work Hubbard established when he founded the project in 2015.

## What Apple Source Integration on FreeBSD Actually Requires

NextBSD's specific work is integrating Apple's open-source Darwin components into FreeBSD. This does not happen automatically: it requires deliberate porting effort each time Apple releases relevant Darwin code. Darwin's being open source makes the code available, but availability is not the same as accessibility across ecosystems. The porting work is what keeps Darwin components circulating in FreeBSD rather than remaining only where Apple's own infrastructure uses them.

The seven-year gap in the original repository's commit history is the visible record of what this work looks like when its maintainer steps back. The project did not close; the last commits simply stopped accumulating, and the gap persisted.

## FreeBSD Infrastructure Fragility and the Seven-Year Gap in Apple Source Coverage

From a systems perspective, the dormancy and revival of NextBSD is a case study in how open-source infrastructure projects that bridge major platform codebasesâ€”Darwin to FreeBSD, in this instanceâ€”depend on continued individual contribution for their continued existence. A seven-year gap in the commit history of an infrastructure bridging project is not merely a record of a pause; it is a record of an absence in the flow of Apple's Darwin code into the FreeBSD ecosystem. The porting work is a dependency, and like other infrastructure dependencies, its status is not fully visible until the maintenance stops.

Maloney's revival restarts the porting work, and the new project history page acknowledges the prior contributors. Whether the revived NextBSD builds a contributor base broad enough to reduce dependency on any single person's continued involvement is a question the new repository's commit history has only begun to answer.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;3tfz0E-3kyFJgvPQNBTmPHvPmm-L9WD1gOu5jPvfbJ8ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;KvJ6s28ljT5I_XfvyQtH3j4o1Obe_nTV75pPTa6agaIƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;4VUzy2G3NHWLJCTg6pom67iAPDkSQAJkMjREWDpnneAƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;UrIGp0GUEonVIpyVQocCXZLBdfyhr_L2Bp_XZbvtza4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxclaude-code-cli-invocationsƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;aZ_cw-otRtwilEuWvR-fzr62qja3hxsVGtyQ2NI_6-Yƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka1ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ikGeQMvHO8k8SJqSHo65bGon4570LyxTuMh7ev2llScƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkf90.761ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;6y-YZIABtnudxsNmfVjCuR_tpBVfVLgG_TtvoUSy7sEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;6zZl7vW_GnoNNl4kNdJduG8RFkLUr71-h8NVhLZHFX8ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;ayQDuRUNPbHeNBMyo9ll3Ryf0DvkKqVBa7rU30H5o_4ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;KUTpF2B8XB56U6puqYxIsLLoCEarGa3wluh7He8Skcwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒeright